"""
battery-announce: spoken battery announcements for SteamOS.

Runs entirely as your user (no root, no Developer Mode). Reads the kernel's
power-supply files, speaks with Piper, plays through PipeWire.

Commands:
  battery-announce run                  main loop (what the service runs)
  battery-announce status               show raw and corrected readings
  battery-announce calibrate <PERCENT>  type the % Steam shows right now
  battery-announce calibrate-gui        calibration window (for the Steam launcher)
  battery-announce reset-calibration    remove the correction
  battery-announce say "some text"      speak a test phrase
  battery-announce test                 speak one of each announcement
  battery-announce now                  speak a readout right now
  battery-announce off | on | toggle    mute / unmute automatic announcements
  battery-announce alerts-gui           alert settings window (for the Steam launcher)
  battery-announce alerts ...           view / change alerts (`alerts help` for details)
"""

# How the pieces fit together
# ---------------------------
#   config    load/save ~/.config/battery-announce/config.json on top of DEFAULTS
#   battery   read /sys/class/power_supply: percentage, charging state, time estimates
#   speech    turn text into a WAV with Piper (cached for repeated phrases) and play it
#   logic     the Announcer class: decides *when* to speak, polled every few seconds
#   commands  one function per command-line verb (run, status, calibrate, now, ...)
#   alerts    editable alert levels and messages, shared by the window and `alerts`
#   windows   the calibration and alert settings windows launched from Steam
#
# Only the Python standard library is used, so nothing has to be installed with pip.

